      "slo_id": "S1",
      "level": "understand",
      "question": "When comparing fractions, where should you write each product from cross multiplication?",
      "options": [
        "Directly under the numerator that made it",
        "Under the denominator of the other fraction",
        "Anywhere, as long as you remember which is which"
      ],
      "correct_index": 0,
      "explanation": "The lesson specifically instructed to write each product directly under the numerator that made it to avoid confusion when comparing.",
      "selected_because": "the teacher's instruction on where to write cross products",
      "distractor_misconceptions": {
        "1": "confuses which product belongs to which fraction",
        "2": "believes placement of products does not matter"
      },
      "option_feedback": {
        "correct": "That's right! Writing each product directly under its corresponding numerator helps you correctly identify which product belongs to which fraction.",
        "wrong": {
          "1": "It's easy to get confused about which product belongs to which fraction. The teacher taught us to write each product directly under the numerator that made it to keep things clear.",
          "2": "While remembering is good, a specific method helps prevent mistakes. The lesson showed us to write each product directly under the numerator that made it, in two different colours, before comparing anything."
